Mating Material Non-IV Batch v1.0.1 — recovery of the reviewed v1.0.0 run

Run RUN_ALL.command from ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop.
Expected runtime on the 12-core MacBook Pro / XT_Pro: approximately 1–2 hours;
allow 2.5 hours on a busy drive. This full-data recovery runtime is an estimate.
The original countdown fit took about 57 minutes. No new engine evaluations,
profile requests, downloads of game data, or Glicko replay are performed.

WHAT THE RETURN SHOWED

The reviewed v1.0.0 run, 99984ef97df55388, took 101.05 minutes. Eight of eleven
families finished: split-half persistence, tenure, arena, first/repeat,
reputation, stakes, K/RD decomposition, and nonparametric rating-gap profiles.
All 231 report-file checksums match the uploaded report manifest.
The first/repeat family retains the same three nonconverged repeat-only
auxiliary models as its archived baseline; its required pooled interaction
and eight estimable models completed. These auxiliary models are not silently
treated as estimates and are not converted into a new specification here.

THIS RECOVERY

1. Authenticate and retain all eight completed families, including their
   original permanent private output checksums. Do not rerun their models.
   Aggregate reports are copied; large private caches stay in the original run.
2. Patron: use fetch_record_batch, the Arrow streaming method supported by
   pinned DuckDB 1.3.2. The SQL, model specification, batch size, coefficient
   calculation, and HC1/chooser-CR1 covariance remain unchanged. Reuse the
   committed rematch and postcertification fits, with their original keys and
   byte checksums. Recreate and check the narrow opportunity cache, then finish
   its three base models and twelve ply sensitivities.
3. Countdown: the old source-stamp check blocked before any model was fit.
   Rebuild the narrow features directly from the authenticated material panel
   using the exact original feasibility projector. The projector uses existing
   FENs and piece counts; it does not call a chess engine. Fit the unchanged
   145 threshold/calendar models with the original covariance and convergence
   checks. Monthly projections and models support checked resume.
4. Responsibility: collect the existing failed run's complete aggregate
   reproduction diagnostics, including covariance arrays. They were omitted
   from the first combined return. Do not rerun the same failing check or relax
   its tolerances. This stage remains REFERENCE_REVIEW_REQUIRED until those
   diagnostics are reviewed. A diagnostic receipt is not analysis completion.

INPUTS AND OUTPUTS

Project root: __PRIVATE_VALUE_1__
Input authority: the reviewed mating_material_first_run_v100_PRIVATE run
 aa7e95f275c18f43; 41,513,719 main opportunities and 570,422 grants.
Both author accounts, __PRIVATE_VALUE_2__ and __PRIVATE_VALUE_3__, remain excluded in both roles.
The original price layer and factual history are preserved.
The reviewed v1.0.0 run must still be present, with its private caches and
native responsibility failure ZIP. Its files are read-only inputs. The launcher
holds its existing run lock while reusing it, preventing simultaneous reruns.

New private output:
derived/replication/mating_material_noniv_batch_v101_PRIVATE/<run key>
This does not overwrite the v1.0.0 run or standalone model outputs.

The launcher uses the existing MatingMaterial_Models_Env_v100 environment.
Dependencies are pinned; the offline tests run before production.
At most ten workers and 11 GB total budget are requested. Countdown uses up to
three projection workers, then up to four fitting workers under its memory
scheduler. Each worker uses one BLAS thread. Families run sequentially.

At the end return the newly printed MATERIAL_NONIV_BATCH_<new key>_RETURN.zip
and its .sha256. The old run's return ZIP is preserved under its original name.
The new combined report includes the eight retained families, Patron/countdown
results or errors, and complete responsibility reproduction diagnostics.
With successful Patron/countdown recovery the status is still BATCH_INCOMPLETE
with ten completed/reused families and one REVIEW_REQUIRED family. Exit code 2
at that point is expected: it does not mean the recovered results were lost.

If interrupted, run the same command again. Authenticated completed families
and committed submodel checkpoints are reused. Changed inputs or corrupt
committed outputs cause an error rather than silent reuse.

WHAT REMAINS AFTER THIS RECOVERY

Responsibility diagnosis; the IV and remaining receipt companions; remaining
recipient-side Patron/adjacent-payoff checks; then manuscript-to-output
reconciliation, table/figure replacement, and compilation of the paper.
This package does not claim the whole-paper rerun is finished.

VALIDATION

The release validation records the exact offline test result. Tests include
actual DuckDB 1.3.2 Arrow streaming, expanded-data coefficient and covariance
comparisons, all fifteen Patron opportunity specifications, committed Patron
fit reuse/corruption checks, all twenty-four countdown months and 145 model
tasks with resume, author-role and material checks, report privacy, and carrying
a failed responsibility check forward as unresolved. Full production outputs
can only be validated from the Mac return.
